1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:29,340
Whoever starts describing that mouse to me again,

3
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:30,300
is getting kicked off the Team!

4
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:31,710
Leo's always sneaking off

5
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:32,700
to practice by himself.

6
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:34,620
So shady.

7
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,980
Mark! You're the Captain!

8
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:39,420
How could you instigate a private Duel like this?

9
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,340
Shake hands right now!

10
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:43,740
If Leo had just shown off his skills
in front of the Coach sooner,

11
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:46,620
Mark never would've become Captain in the first place.

12
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,540
This kind of Duel,

13
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:49,980
instigated out of pure ego and pride,

14
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:52,380
is incredibly damaging to Team unity.

15
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:53,820
You understand?

16
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Episode 11

17
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,540
The next Training Activity

18
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:02,940
is a 1-day trip to the Ancient Town!

19
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:06,780
Coach, are you talking in your sleep?

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,180
You must have said the wrong thing.

21
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:10,620
Do you think I'm like you?

22
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,980
We need to balance work and rest.

23
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:16,380
So today, I'm giving you guys the day off.

24
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,780
We're heading to the Ancient Town next to Falcon Camp

25
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,670
for a full day of fun. How's that sound?

26
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:21,660
Yay!

27
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,100
Coach, you're a genius!

28
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,540
Long live the Coach!

29
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:25,980
Coach, we'll love you forever!

30
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:27,300
Hey!

31
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:29,970
Okay, now that's just getting weird.

32
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:32,220
Alright, breakfast time!

33
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:43,230
These houses are built with grey bricks and white tiles.

34
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,180
The street food in this Ancient Town is up ahead,

35
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:46,620
you've had enough, haven't you?

36
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,500
We've barely eaten anything yet.

37
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:50,940
This one's good.

38
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:04,880
Smile! Come on, smile!

39
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:23,100
Leo, can you take a picture of me and my Sister?

40
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:24,540
Hold still.

41
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,600
Nice.

42
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:36,540
Captain.

43
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:38,460
Stop thinking about that Duel with Leo.

44
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,960
Let's just enjoy this day to the fullest, okay?

45
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:43,260
Right now,

46
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:46,140
This isn't just about a single Duel anymore.

47
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,460
The situation is far more serious than that.

48
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Don't you get it?

49
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:53,300
What is it?

50
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,280
They like following Leo around.

51
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:56,620
So just let them follow him.

52
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:57,960
What's the worst that could happen?

53
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,060
Don't be so naive, alright?

54
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,460
Mickey's already inciting everyone

55
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:03,900
to vote for a new Captain.

56
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,780
Don't you have any sense of vigilance at all?

57
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:07,740
That little squirt.

58
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,660
I don't even consider him a threat.

59
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:12,540
You're still too naive.

60
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,920
Can't you see who's really pulling the
strings behind that little squirt?

61
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,340
You mean Mini?

62
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,780
Then there's even less to be worried of.

63
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:22,140
Oh, come on.
Are you really that dense, or just pretending?

64
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,060
How could it be Mini?

65
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:25,500
Obviously, it's Leo.

66
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:28,860
Only Leo has a real shot at running for Captain.

67
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,360
I never realized Leo was so sneaky and underhanded.

68
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:32,700
That little rascal.

69
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:37,020
You know what they say: "A barking dog never bites."

70
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,940
You're only figuring this out now?

71
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,340
I think I'm gonna head back to Base first.

72
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:42,780
You guys take your time.

73
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:45,180
Captain, we finally get a day off.

74
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:46,620
Why go back to Base?

75
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:48,540
The Captain's not exactly in a great mood like you are.

76
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:52,860
Captain, you want us to head back with you?

77
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,700
Nah, it's fine.
You guys stay and have fun.

78
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:58,620
I just want some time alone.

79
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:12,540
Leo, hurry up!

80
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:18,300
Look over there!

81
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:29,820
Chuck, how come you ended up at this restaurant again?

82
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,260
Weren't you just at the dumpling place?

83
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:35,620
"A tree moved dies, a man moved thrives."

84
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,020
What kind of nonsense is that?

85
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,380
You just love misusing words.

86
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,820
I'm leaving these 2 bags here with you.

87
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:43,740
I still need to go ahead

88
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:45,180
and check out the hat shop.

89
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:46,620
Popcorn.

90
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:49,020
Can you please stop buying stuff non-stop?

91
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,860
I can barely carry all this anymore.

92
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,790
Oh, come on. Carrying more helps with digestion.

93
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,260
That way you can eat even more.

94
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:57,180
I don't need your help with my digestion.

95
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:58,620
I can eat plenty on my own.

96
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,060
Alright, alright.

97
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:02,280
I know your stomach is practically a bottomless pit.

98
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,780
But could you please muster up
just a tiny shred of responsibility

99
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:05,820
and help me out here? Please?

100
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,260
Okay, okay, okay.

101
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:14,500
And remember, don't just focus on stuffing your face.
Keep an eye on my stuff.

102
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:19,740
So annoying.

103
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,660
The hardest thing to endure in life

104
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,580
is people bothering me while I'm eating.

105
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,780
Sis, there's a bench over there. Let's take a break.

106
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,780
Leo, the scenery here is really nice.

107
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:45,660
Can you take another picture of me and my sister?

108
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:46,290
Sure.

109
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:47,580
You two go stand over there.

110
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,460
A little closer. Closer.

111
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:53,820
Shawn.

112
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:55,260
What's wrong?

113
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:58,140
Quick! Hurry! That huge yellow dog is chasing after us!

114
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,500
There's nothing there!

115
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:04,860
Shawn, maybe it's just because you're so scared of dogs

116
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:07,260
that you're hallucinating.

117
00:07:07,650 --> 00:07:08,680
It really was a huge yellow dog!

118
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,540
I was just about to have a nice chat with it,

119
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,940
but then it just locked its eyes on me

120
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:15,900
and started chasing me!

121
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:20,700
Having a heart-to-heart with a big yellow dog?
Shawn, you're hilarious.

122
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,100
I think they make a great pair.

123
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:24,510
What?

124
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:25,980
Communication is my specialty, after all.

125
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:29,340
Oh man, here we go again.

126
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:37,980
This guy...

127
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,820
Let's go.
Come on, let's go.

128
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,420
It's the Chengnan Team.
What are they doing here?

129
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:07,260
Don't tell me they're Training at Falcon Camp too?

130
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:08,700
Very likely.

131
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:12,350
Didn't Monica say last time that they've got great gear

132
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:13,500
and plenty of funding?

133
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:15,920
I bet they're here for a Training Camp, too.

134
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,300
Hey! Jianghai Team!

135
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:20,700
What are you whispering about over there?

136
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,620
You're the ones whispering!

137
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:25,500
We come here first, and you guys show up right after.

138
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,900
Who's following you?

139
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:30,300
I could just as easily say you're the ones following us.

140
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:34,600
And if I said you were following us,
I'd actually have a good reason for it.

141
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:36,060
What reason?

142
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:41,340
We were the Champions last year.
You guys were just the Runner-Ups.

143
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:45,180
It's only natural for the
Runner-Ups to follow the Champions.

144
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:48,060
Hey! What are you saying?

145
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:52,860
Mark might've won a Championship, but that's just him.

146
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:55,260
The rest of you rookies are just riding his coattails!

147
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:59,580
That's right! The Team Competition was only added this year!

148
00:09:00,220 --> 00:09:01,800
So we'll just have to see which Team comes out on top!

149
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:03,900
It'll obviously be our Team!

150
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:07,260
Other than that Mark guy,

151
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:10,620
who can only do a few tricks anyways,
what else do you have?

152
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,020
That's a pretty arrogant thing to say.

153
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,900
Besides that Runner-Up title, what else have you got?

154
00:09:20,050 --> 00:09:20,700
Originally,

155
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:23,100
I was gonna teach you guys a lesson today.

156
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,980
But considering your so-called "Champion" isn't here,

157
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,820
I'll let it slide.
Otherwise you'd just say we're bullying the weak.

158
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Let's go.

159
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:33,180
Hold up.

160
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,910
You don't need to be so polite with us.

161
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:41,180
If you wanna battle, let's just battle.

162
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:44,700
Whoever's got the guts, step right up.

163
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:48,060
I'm the weakest one on our Team,

164
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:51,900
but I'm still more than enough to take any of you on.

165
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:55,260
You've got a big mouth.

166
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,660
I'm the weakest one on our Team, too.

167
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,990
But I'm more than enough to deal with you.

168
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:02,460
Bring it on!

169
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:03,420
Bring it!

170
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:27,700
[Name: Zoe | Team: Chengnan]
[Yo-Yo: Sky Fiend | Special Move: Sky Fiend Whirlwind]

171
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:21,660
Let's settle this with 1 Final Move.
Deal?

172
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:23,100
Whatever.

173
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:24,540
Take this!

174
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:58,620
We called you rookies and you didn't believe us.

175
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:00,540
Now look at you.

176
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,940
You can't even beat a girl from our Team.

177
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:04,860
All you so-called "men" just stand there

178
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,260
while a girl does all the fighting for you?

179
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,620
I think you're the real rookies here.

180
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:13,500
Sounds like you're not convinced.

181
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,010
Of course I'm not.

182
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:16,380
Why should I be?

183
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:18,780
Real men don't fight girls.

184
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:22,140
But I'm right here waiting to take you both on.

185
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:25,500
That's a pretty bold claim.
Taking on two of us?

186
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:31,260
You'll have to get past me first.

187
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:35,100
Fine. Be my guest.

188
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:04,000
[Name: Hugo | Team: Chengnan]
[Yo-Yo: Ice Crack | Special Move: Invincible Ice Fissure]

189
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:25,980
Ah! My Yo-Yo!

190
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:30,780
Teddy, you...

191
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,660
I didn't do it on purpose.

192
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,060
Your skills just aren't up to par.

193
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:37,020
How dare you!

194
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,900
Looks like I'll have to teach you a lesson.

195
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:41,340
Well, if that's how you want it.

196
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:42,940
There's nothing I can do about that.

197
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:44,700
Then let's go!

198
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:46,620
Fine. Don't regret it.

199
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:04,380
I'll only need 1 move to take you down.

200
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:09,660
Beating you... I never even planned on needing a 2nd move.

201
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:16,000
[Name: Jacky | Team: Chengnan Captain]
[Yo-Yos: Coiling Dragon / Mystic Wind Dance]
[Special Move: Coiling Dragon Tornado]

202
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,600
Centrifugal Vortex!

203
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:26,480
Coiling Dragon Tornado!

204
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:54,300
Still not convinced?

205
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:58,140
Then go get Mark and have him come face me!

206
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:05,340
That's the price you pay for destroying my Ice Crack.

207
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:10,140
Matthew.

208
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:13,730
Matthew!
I can't believe I ran into you here.

209
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:14,940
Who are you?

210
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:18,300
I'm Zoe, your old Elementary School Classmate.

211
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:23,100
What's wrong with your eyes?
You still can't recognize me?

212
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:26,460
Zoe?

213
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:27,390
Yeah.

214
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,340
The one who'd kick your chair every time we argued?

215
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:30,780
Back then, you always said

216
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:34,140
that "Even the finest horse sometimes stumbles."

217
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:35,100
That was you?

218
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,300
You remember now?

219
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:39,420
Just remember: during a Match, we're Opponents.

220
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:41,350
But once it's over, we're friends again. Here.

221
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:43,740
What are you doing?

222
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,540
That should help you remember me! Bye!

223
00:16:53,780 --> 00:16:55,750
They didn't send her to pull some kind of
honeytrap on us, did they?

224
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,580
Ah, forget it.

225
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:01,500
Let's just head back to Base. Let's go.

226
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:03,900
You scored the biggest haul today.

227
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,300
Everything we're carrying is your stuff.

228
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:08,670
Chuck's haul is just as big as mine.

229
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:10,140
Only his is all inside his stomach.

230
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,540
My haul is just like Leo's.

231
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:13,980
Totally invisible.

232
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:15,420
Nonsense.

233
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,340
Leo spent the whole time listening to my
Sister talk about the Ancient Town.

234
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,260
Not like you, just stuffing your face non-stop.

235
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:22,590
Yeah, he actually gained some knowledge.

236
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:25,500
Doesn't that kind of gain count as invisible?

237
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:28,860
Chuck, that was actually a pretty smart thing to say.

238
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:31,740
After eating all that food,
it's about time his brain grew a little.

239
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:35,100
Did you guys get to see much of the Ancient Town?

240
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,020
I bought a ton of pork chops!

241
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:41,340
Let's go back and visit again!

242
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:43,740
What's going on here?

243
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:58,140
Matthew, what's the meaning of this?

244
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,540
Why is all our luggage out here?

245
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,460
Is the Training Camp Cancelled?

246
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:04,860
You wish.

247
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:07,260
What's going on?

248
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,180
Listen up, everyone.

249
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:12,060
Don't panic. Don't panic.

250
00:18:13,180 --> 00:18:14,460
What on Earth is happening?

251
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:18,300
Here's the situation.

252
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:22,140
Due to a number of different reasons,

253
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:25,500
the Funding from the School didn't come through in time.

254
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:31,740
And the Sponsorships I was trying to
secure didn't pan out either.

255
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:36,540
So we can't afford to pay the Base
the fees for the cabins anymore.

256
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:40,380
New guests are checking into the cabins tomorrow.

257
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:43,060
So for the time being, we have to move out.

258
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:45,660
Coach.

259
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:50,940
So what do we do now?

260
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,300
I've already talked it over with the Base Management.

261
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:55,710
They've agreed

262
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:57,660
to let us keep using the Training Grounds.

263
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:59,100
And as for tonight,

264
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:02,460
we're gonna be camping out in tents.

265
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:05,260
Ugh, that's even worse than the cabins!

266
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:08,220
Are there snakes out there?

267
00:19:08,300 --> 00:19:09,300
Ah!

268
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:11,580
Mickey, stop making stuff up.

269
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:15,900
Actually, what I meant was, are there gonna be mosquitoes?

270
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:16,860
Oh no. Oh no.

271
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:19,260
Mosquitoes love biting me the most!

272
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:21,400
Well, they sure won't be biting me.

273
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:23,100
Not me, either.

274
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:26,460
Whoa, have a little sympathy, would you?

275
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,340
Coach, if we can't sleep well at night,

276
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:31,260
our Training during the day will be totally useless.

277
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:35,580
Let's not all just focus on the negatives, alright?

278
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:37,980
I think this will actually help forge our willpower even more.

279
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:40,780
And it'll help us achieve the
real purpose of this Training Camp.

280
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:41,820
Right?

281
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,940
Mickey, that's not gonna help.

282
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:53,340
You're just annoying the mosquitoes.

283
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:54,600
And once you lie down,

284
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:56,220
they're gonna come back and attack you even harder.

285
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:58,140
Yeah! You're driving those mosquitoes crazy!

286
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:00,060
So I'm just gonna suffer even more?

287
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:01,500
What am I supposed to do about it?

288
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:02,430
The second I lie down,

289
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:04,380
the mosquitoes just start buzzing right in my ear!

290
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:05,340
It's so annoying!

291
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:10,620
Ugh. Well, what do you expect when we
don't have enough funding for Training?

292
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:13,500
Alright, alright, enough already.

293
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:15,420
Mickey.

294
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:18,780
Those mosquitoes are already doing
you a favor by just buzzing.

295
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:20,700
For me, I haven't even laid down yet

296
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:23,100
and they're already biting me all over!

